WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.110 align:start position:0%
 
park  an oasis of green in the heart of the  city  it runs along an old rail line that once  ran south from potsdamer platz  it covers an area totaling 26 000 square  meters  that means there's lots of room for all  kinds of activities  it's so central i can get here from but  in no time  i like the wide variety of playgrounds  it's such a wonderful place for older  people to come for a stroll but young  people too  you can still see some of the old tracks  you can only guess at what used to go on  here  old tracks that are overgrown  these relics of pre-war days were  deliberately left in place and  integrated into the park  a century ago this was europe's largest  railway complex consisting of the amhata  station and a freight depot  the junction of all these lines was  called gleiss drayek or triangle of  rails  the rail lines and stations were  completely destroyed in the second world  war the area became part of west berlin  but the rights to use the railway  facilities went to east germany which  left the property unused  in the 1960s locals started pushing to  have the area around kleistraeck  developed one of them was klaus trapman  now for their  it was actually fenced off  but starting in the 60s and 70s  little groups of nature lovers started  coming here  after germany was reunified the berlin  senate considered putting a highway  through gleistraeck but a citizens  initiative proposed turning it into a  park in 2004 they got their way  citizens city planners and architects  work together to design a metropolitan  park  its railway history still can be  experienced in many places  the ideas and needs of ordinary  berliners were taken into consideration  when creating the park  that's why the park includes a 1300  square meter skatepark developed in  consultation with active skaters  gleistraeck park once the largest  railway complex in europe  it's now a place of recreation and  relaxation  an example of how something special can  rise out of ruins

